# Validation

- No pytest. Use `validate_system.py` or a sibling direct runner.
- Every run writes a terminal readout plus JSON and Markdown artifacts under `test/system/runs/<timestamp>/`.
- Distinguish component checks from end-to-end production-path checks in the report language.
- A green check that does not exercise `PluginManager.load_plugin()` is not a plugin-system proof.
- Harness host stand-ins stay in the validation runner. They never enter `host_protocols.py`.
